  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. A call for ideas regarding AI-enhanced data visualization was issued with a July 20th deadline. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. The project reached a milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase and prototype testing for secure file sharing, ahead of schedule. A celebration is planned for October 10th, with UI enhancements planned for October. Security protocols, including MFA and encryption, are being updated effective January next year. The executive board approved a total budget of $2M, and a separate $15,000 budget for training programs was approved, with sessions starting next month."
